  "description": "LIRRIQ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C140 H144 Eu4 N12 O16,C2 H3 N1. From the CIF bond table, Eu1 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu2 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu1A (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu2A (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu3 (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu4 (Eu) has 6 O neighbors; Eu3A (Eu) has 7 O neighbors; Eu4A (Eu) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.633-3.958 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 96.97-112.36°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Eu4(μ3-OH)2(tmhd)4L6]·2CH3CN (C144H150Eu4N14O16). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
